### 2. LiveData

**Theory:**

LiveData is an observable data holder that:
- Respects app lifecycle (only updates active observers)
- Prevents memory leaks
- Automatically unsubscribes when lifecycle ends
- Holds single value, emits when changed

**Types of LiveData:**

```kotlin
// MutableLiveData - can be changed from outside
val mutableUser = MutableLiveData<User>()
mutableUser.value = user

// Immutable exposure - only internal can change
private val _user = MutableLiveData<User>()
val user: LiveData<User> = _user

// Transformations
val userNameLength = user.map { it.name.length }
val adultUsers = users.switchMap { userList ->
    filterByAge(userList, 18)
}

// Combined data
val userInfo = Transformations.switchMap(userId) { id ->
    userRepository.getUser(id)
}
```

**Implementation:**

```kotlin
class UserViewModel : ViewModel() {
    // Expose as read-only LiveData
    private val _userList = MutableLiveData<List<User>>()
    val userList: LiveData<List<User>> = _userList
    
    // Transformations
    val userCount: LiveData<Int> = userList.map { it.size }
    
    val adultUsers: LiveData<List<User>> = userList.map { users ->
        users.filter { it.age >= 18 }
    }
    
    fun loadUsers() {
        viewModelScope.launch {
            _userList.value = fetchUsers()
        }
    }
}

// Observe in Activity
class UserActivity : AppCompatActivity() {
    private val viewModel: UserViewModel by viewModels()
    
    override fun onCreate(savedInstanceState: Bundle?) {
        super.onCreate(savedInstanceState)
        
        // Only receives updates while activity is at least STARTED
        viewModel.userList.observe(this) { users ->
            displayUsers(users)
        }
        
        // Access transformed data
        viewModel.userCount.observe(this) { count ->
            showUserCount("Total: $count")
        }
    }
}
```

**LiveData Lifecycle Behavior:**

```kotlin
// ✓ Receives updates (active)
lifecycle state: STARTED, RESUMED
observer.onChanged(value)

// ✗ Doesn't receive updates (inactive)
lifecycle state: CREATED, DESTROYED
// observer not called, but still observing

// Remove observer when lifecycle ends
// Automatic with lifecycle-aware observe()
viewModel.data.observe(this) { ... }  // Auto-unsubscribes at onDestroy
```

