### Flow & Reactive Programming

**Theory:**
Flow is a Kotlin coroutine-based API for reactive streams.

**Flow vs LiveData:**

```
LiveData:
├── Lifecycle-aware
├── Hot observable
├── Simple for UI
└── Android-specific

Flow:
├── Not lifecycle-aware
├── Cold observable
├── Powerful transformations
└── Pure Kotlin
```

**Implementation:**

```kotlin
// Producer
class UserRepository {
    fun getUsers(): Flow<List<User>> = flow {
        try {
            // Emit initial local data
            val cached = userDao.getAllUsers()
            emit(cached)
            
            // Fetch fresh data
            val fresh = userApi.getUsers()
            userDao.insertAll(fresh)
            emit(fresh)
        } catch (e: Exception) {
            // Handle error
        }
    }
    
    // Reactive database query
    fun observeUser(id: String): Flow<User> {
        return userDao.observeUser(id)
            .map { entity ->
                entity.toDomain()
            }
    }
}

// ViewModel
@HiltViewModel
class UserViewModel @Inject constructor(
    private val repository: UserRepository
) : ViewModel() {
    
    // Convert Flow to LiveData
    val users: LiveData<List<User>> = 
        repository.getUsers().asLiveData()
    
    // Or keep as Flow
    val userUpdates: Flow<User> = 
        MutableStateFlow("").switchMap { id ->
            repository.observeUser(id)
        }
}

// UI Layer
class UserFragment : Fragment() {
    
    override fun onViewCreated(view: View, savedInstanceState: Bundle?) {
        // Method 1: With LiveData
        viewModel.users.observe(viewLifecycleOwner) { users ->
            updateUI(users)
        }
        
        // Method 2: With Flow + lifecycleScope
        viewLifecycleOwner.lifecycleScope.launch {
            repeatOnLifecycle(Lifecycle.State.STARTED) {
                viewModel.userUpdates.collect { user ->
                    updateUI(user)
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

**Flow Operators:**

```kotlin
repository.getUsers()
    // Transformation
    .map { users ->
        users.sortedBy { it.name }
    }
    // Filtering
    .filter { users ->
        users.isNotEmpty()
    }
    // Flattening
    .flatMapLatest { users ->
        repository.getDetails(users)
    }
    // Error handling
    .catch { error ->
        emit(emptyList())
    }
    // Side effects
    .onEach { users ->
        logger.log("Users: ${users.size}")
    }
    .collect { users ->
        updateUI(users)
    }
```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ Cold observable - new instance per collector
- ✅ Powerful operators: map, filter, flatMap, catch
- ✅ Coroutine-based, not lifecycle-aware
- ✅ Convert to LiveData for safe UI updates
- ✅ Use in repository and ViewModel layers

