## Architecture Components

### ViewModel Deep Dive

**Theory:**
ViewModel is designed to survive configuration changes and hold UI-related data.

**How ViewModel Survives Rotation:**

```
Device Rotation Event:
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Activity destroyed (onDestroy called)   │
│ BUT ViewModel instance persists         │
│ Framework re-creates Activity           │
│ ViewModel data still there              │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘

Without ViewModel:
onCreate() → fetch users (AGAIN)
onCreate() → fetch users (AGAIN)
onCreate() → fetch users (AGAIN)
[Wasteful API calls, UI flicker]

With ViewModel:
onCreate() → fetch users (1st time)
[Rotation - Activity destroyed]
onCreate() → get cached users [No API call]
```

**Implementation:**

```kotlin
@HiltViewModel
class UserListViewModel @Inject constructor(
    private val repository: UserRepository,
    private val logger: Logger
) : ViewModel() {
    
    // Mutable internally, exposed as immutable
    private val _users = MutableLiveData<List<User>>()
    val users: LiveData<List<User>> = _users
    
    private val _isLoading = MutableLiveData<Boolean>()
    val isLoading: LiveData<Boolean> = _isLoading
    
    private val _error = MutableLiveData<String?>()
    val error: LiveData<String?> = _error
    
    // Lazy initialization
    private val userComparator = compareBy<User> { it.name }
    
    // Called once when ViewModel created
    init {
        loadUsers()
    }
    
    fun loadUsers() {
        viewModelScope.launch {
            _isLoading.value = true
            
            try {
                val users = repository.getUsers()
                _users.value = users.sortedWith(userComparator)
                _error.value = null
                logger.log("Users loaded: ${users.size}")
            } catch (e: Exception) {
                _error.value = e.message
                logger.error("Load failed", e)
            } finally {
                _isLoading.value = false
            }
        }
    }
    
    // Clean up when ViewModel destroyed
    override fun onCleared() {
        super.onCleared()
        logger.log("UserListViewModel cleared")
        // Cancel long-running operations if needed
    }
}
```

**Usage:**

```kotlin
class UserListFragment : Fragment() {
    
    // ViewModels are tied to Fragment lifecycle
    private val viewModel: UserListViewModel by viewModels()
    
    override fun onViewCreated(view: View, savedInstanceState: Bundle?) {
        super.onViewCreated(view, savedInstanceState)
        
        // Observe with viewLifecycleOwner
        viewModel.users.observe(viewLifecycleOwner) { users ->
            adapter.submitList(users)
        }
        
