## Quick Reference

### Lifecycle Events Flowchart

```
Activity/Fragment Created
         ↓
    onCreate()
         ↓
    onStart()
         ↓
    onResume() ← Can interact
         ↓
  [User navigates away]
         ↓
    onPause()
         ↓
    onStop()
         ↓
   onDestroy()
         ↓
    [Destroyed]
```

### Data Flow

```
User Action
    ↓
Fragment calls ViewModel.action()
    ↓
ViewModel calls Repository
    ↓
Repository queries Database OR API
    ↓
Data flows back through Flow/LiveData
    ↓
Fragment observes and updates UI
```

### Coroutine Scope Cancellation

```
App Lifetime:
  ├─ GlobalScope (Never cancelled) ❌ Avoid
  │
  ├─ App Scope
  │  └─ Activity/Fragment created
  │     ├─ viewModelScope (Auto-cancelled)
  │     └─ lifecycleScope (Auto-cancelled)
```

